Chapter: ActTcoLoop

 An effectful act loop must be constant-stack. spin is the shape of an
 interactive poll loop: an act block that binds a conditional device
 read, then tail-calls itself. The bind before the tail call is the
 regression trigger -- emit-act-stmts once threaded the cleared
 tail-position flag from the bind into the final statement, so the self
 call compiled as a real call and the stack grew every iteration.

 The heap is advanced to about 115 MB below the 3 GB stack top before
 the loop runs, so a non-TCO build collides stack into heap within two
 million iterations and halts; a constant-stack build finishes four
 million iterations in well under a second. The margin assumes the
 default 3072 MB test VM.

Section: Main

  spin : Integer -> [Device.Port] Integer
  spin (i) = act
   status <- if i == 0 then port-in-byte 128 else 0
   if i <= 0 then status else spin (i - 1)
  end

  opening : [Console, Device.Port] Nothing = act
   adv <- __heap-advance 3100000000
   r <- spin 4000000
   print-line-uni "ACT-TCO-OK"
  end
